---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';

const path = '/use-cases/reviews-and-ugc';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/reviews-and-ugc');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/reviews-and-ugc');
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/use-cases" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Use reviews and customer content responsibly</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">Separate asking for an honest review from obtaining permission to reuse a photograph or quotation in recovery messages.</p>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mt-12 max-w-4xl p-8">
      <h2>Ask after a relevant experience</h2>
      <p>Choose a request point appropriate to delivery and meaningful product use, with a fallback when those milestones are unknown. Avoid repeated asks for the same order from different tools. Customers with a problem need a support route, but dissatisfaction should not be used to filter who is allowed to leave an honest review.</p>
      <h2>Track permission separately</h2>
      <p>A submitted review and permission to republish a customer image are different records. Record the intended channels, approved asset and withdrawal contact before reuse. Have the operator review applicable rights and incentive rules; this workflow is not a legal determination. Do not condition a reward on a positive opinion.</p>
      <h2>Keep proof relevant and intact</h2>
      <p>Match review excerpts to the actual product or variant and retain context that changes their meaning. Do not turn a customer statement into a verified performance claim. If content is removed or permission changes, identify which templates and campaigns contain the asset so an owner can replace it.</p>
      <h2>Evaluate the content handoff</h2>
      <p>Ask a review provider and messaging candidate to demonstrate how approved text, attribution and image permissions reach the editor. Check the empty state for a product with no suitable reviews. A product should not be excluded from receiving honest reviews simply because it has too few today.</p>
      <h2>Proposed acceptance exercise</h2>
      <p>Use an approved staff asset to trace request, approval, insertion and withdrawal. Preview a message after that asset becomes unavailable and confirm a useful fallback. Measure request completion separately from downstream recovery contribution; neither proves that reused content caused additional purchases without an appropriate comparison.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
